{
  "_readme": "Every monster in the game. Edit this file, then run Prince's Palace > Build Default Content in the Unity Editor to regenerate. Only id, displayName, and maxHealth are required — everything else auto-derives a reasonable default if left out (see EnemyEntryResolver.cs for the exact formulas). An attack matching any listed weakness deals +50% damage; one matching any listed resistance deals -50%. Matching several weaknesses at once is impossible (an attack carries one type), so listing more elements widens what hurts a monster rather than deepening it, and no element may appear in both lists. minFloor is a MINIMUM, not a band — a floor-5 room still rolls rats, and the difficulty curve is what keeps it dangerous there; see RawEnemyEntry.minFloor's own comment for the room-length measurements that motivated banding the pool at all. Set isBoss to true only for monsters that should appear exclusively in the dungeon's final room; a boss room draws from every boss whose minFloor it has reached, so which bosses a depth can field is decided entirely by this list — there is no separate per-biome boss table. Field-by-field documentation, defaults and valid enum values: docs/CONTENT_SCHEMA.md.",
